    "result_text": "All 64 tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key and duplicate detection to match the spec.\n\n**`Owner.getIdentityKey()`** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 now returns the SHA-256 digest (64 lowercase hex chars) of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`, replacing the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId`. Added a self-contained American **Soundex** implementation (`Owner.soundex(...)`) plus the SHA-256 hashing, so the last name contributes only its phonetic code and the postcode/household no longer factor into the key.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n- The single `identityKey` equality check remains the only 409 duplicate test (still skipping soft-deleted owners, still after the email-domain blocklist which runs earlier at request time).\n- **Removed the separate household-duplicate 409 block** (keyed on the computed `householdId`). The `householdId` is still computed and `householdMembers` is still gathered \u2014 it now feeds only household size and the membership-level cap, never a rejection.\n- **`findPossibleDuplicate`** now triggers a soft match when `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode match while the whole identity key **differs** (returning the lowest-id match), instead of the old \"same normalized last name + postcode + different telephone\".\n- Removed the now-unused `introducesDistinctEmail` helper and refreshed the surrounding comments.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, and `possibleDuplicateOf` field descriptions/example to reflect the new SHA-256/Soundex formula.\n\nBehavioral effect, confirmed by the acceptance tests: two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones are now created as a soft match (`possibleDuplicate: true`) rather than rejected (Cp10, Cp35), a full identity repeat still collides with 409 (Cp03, Cp25), and the key is a 64-hex SHA-256 value (Cp28, Cp52).",
